API-11: apply a MIN_SLOPE set after open to the conduit slopes

swmm_options_set(e, "MIN_SLOPE", ...) is documented as valid before
swmm_engine_start() and stores the percent, but the minimum slope is
applied when resolve_cross_references() computes the conduit slopes during
swmm_engine_open(). A value set afterwards changed nothing.

In the OPENED state, recompute every conduit's slope with
recompute_conduit_slope() (added by API-10) after MIN_SLOPE is set.

Requires: API-10

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after API-10_swmm600.patch:
    git apply API-11_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/openswmm_model_impl.cpp b/src/engine/core/openswmm_model_impl.cpp
index 8ab54ad..b892ca0 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/openswmm_model_impl.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/openswmm_model_impl.cpp
@@ -1470,7 +1470,14 @@ SWMM_ENGINE_API int swmm_options_set(SWMM_Engine engine,
     else if (k == "LAT_FLOW_TOL")      opt.lat_flow_tol        = stod_strict(v) / 100.0;
     else if (k == "SYS_FLOW_TOL")      opt.sys_flow_tol        = stod_strict(v) / 100.0;
     else if (k == "MIN_SURFAREA")      opt.min_surf_area       = stod_strict(v);
-    else if (k == "MIN_SLOPE")         opt.min_slope           = stod_strict(v);
+    else if (k == "MIN_SLOPE") {
+        opt.min_slope = stod_strict(v);
+        // the minimum applies to the conduit slopes resolved at open
+        auto& ctx = to_engine(engine)->context();
+        if (ctx.state == openswmm::EngineState::OPENED)
+            for (int j = 0; j < ctx.n_links(); ++j)
+                openswmm::input::recompute_conduit_slope(ctx, j);
+    }
     else if (k == "THREADS")           opt.num_threads         = stoi_strict(v);
 
     // Explicit finite-volume solver. Same value grammar as the [OPTIONS]
